> `inspect.unwrap(object)`: Unwrap the given object. If the object has a `__wrapped__` attribute, it is unwrapped recursively until an object without a `__wrapped__` attribute is found.

So `inspect.unwrap(self.call)` already handles `functools.wraps`.

The issue is that `inspect.unwrap` does NOT handle `functools.partial`.

